        <mxCell id="c86" value="By design: expected, record it" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="552.184" y="504" width="166.076" height="24" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c87" value="&lt;i&gt;Four of the eight findings touch two dimensions, so name the one the test examines and add the second when it applies. The In Transit rows conflict only if DeliveryDate records the actual delivery, and are overdue if it is expected. The small periods look like missing transactions (completeness), and sit at the edges of the extract (timeliness), which explains their size without showing that the records are complete. The counts are in the tutorial guides.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="538" width="860" height="72" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
